      "sequence_position": 7,
      "problem": "Given the cubic function $f(x;a,b,c)=a{x}^{3}+b{x}^{2}+cx,$ compute ${∇}_{a,c}\\,f.$\n\n<table align=\"center\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td rowspan=\"2\" width=\"30px\" height=\"35px\" align=\"center\">${∇}_{a,c}\\,f=\\text{ }$</td>\n<td width=\"5px\" height=\"30px\" align=\"center\"></td>\n<td width=\"30px\" align=\"center\">{{field-1}}</td>\n\n<td width=\"5px\" align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr>\n\n<tr> \n<td height=\"35px\" align=\"center\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-2}}</td>\n\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>",
      "worked_solution": "To compute ${∇}_{a,c}\\,f$, we take partial derivatives with respect to $a$ and $c.$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂a} & =\\frac{∂}{∂a}(a{x}^{3}+b{x}^{2}+cx)={x}^{3} \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂c} & =\\frac{∂}{∂c}(a{x}^{3}+b{x}^{2}+cx)=x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∇}_{a,c}\\,f & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂a} \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂c}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}{x}^{3} \\\\ x\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$",
